Package: svngit
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         subversion
Description: run git commands against a Subversion repository
 svngit sits between you and a Subversion working copy. You run git status,
 git add, git commit and git push; it translates each one into the equivalent
 svn command, runs it, and prints the result the way git would have.
 .
 Nothing about the repository changes: colleagues keep using svn, the server
 stays a Subversion server, and there is no mirror or import step. It emulates
 the parts Subversion has no counterpart for -- a staging area, a queue of
 unpushed commits, and a stash -- in state kept outside the working copy.
 .
 A shim is included so that plain "git" works inside Subversion checkouts. It
 is not installed into the PATH by default, because that would shadow the real
 git; run "svngit --shim-path" to opt in.
